<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="content-inventory"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Make a private inventory</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">List the content you would notice if it were missing: contacts, recent and older photos, messages, local documents, downloads, notes, recordings, app-specific records and access to authenticator apps. This is an inventory for your own checking, not a request to share secret information.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Account access matters as much as copied files. Confirm privately that you know the required account sign-in details and can complete the ordinary recovery method if prompted. Do not write passwords, one-time codes or banking and myGov details into a transfer checklist.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Some apps store important records in their own account or service. Others keep data locally or require a vendor-specific sign-in. Treat the app as a separate item to verify later rather than assuming its presence on the destination proves that its records came across.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "Do not expose account secrets") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Keep passwords, recovery codes, authenticator details and banking or myGov operations private. This preparation page does not replace the official recovery process for any provider.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="backup-scope"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Check the latest backup and sync state</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">On Apple devices, Apple’s documented route is Settings, your name, iCloud, iCloud Backup, then Back Up Now. Stay connected until the process completes and check the last successful backup time shown below the control. Read <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.apple.com/en-au/108366">Apple’s iCloud backup guidance</a> for the current labels. Existing iCloud storage limits may affect completion; do not automatically buy storage or delete source content just to make room.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">On Android, Google’s documented route is Settings, Google, All services, then Backup under Backup and restore, followed by Backup now. Labels can vary by device and software version. Review Backup details as well as the completion state. Some apps do not restore every setting or piece of data, and a backup from a higher Android version cannot be restored to a lower one. See <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.google.com/android/answer/2819582?hl=en">Google’s Android backup guidance</a>.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Backup and synchronisation complement each other. <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.apple.com/en-au/108770">Apple’s explanation of iCloud sync and backup</a> is useful when deciding what to verify separately. Do not switch off backups or delete sources to clear space.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "A completed backup has a limited meaning") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">It confirms the reported backup state, not that every app record, download, message or account session will be restored.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="transfer-conditions"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Make the conditions workable</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Charge both devices and keep a compatible cable available if the chosen method needs one. Use reliable Wi-Fi and check that the destination has enough storage for the planned content. Review current software and device compatibility before starting; there is no fixed transfer duration and no universal upgrade requirement.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Do not begin by resetting the new device or erasing the old one. If the destination is already in use, assess its existing data first. If the source is broken, locked, or suspected to be compromised, pause the ordinary transfer and contact the relevant device specialist, manufacturer or account provider.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A transfer may leave downloads, cloud content or app setup pending. Keep a short private list of what still needs checking after the copy process. That list is more useful than relying on a single completion screen.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "Do not clear space by deleting the source") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Keep the original content available until the new device has passed representative checks and any separate account or provider steps are complete.</p>{% endcall %}
